From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 12:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] clk: cix: sky1: reject partial CLKT maps

The CLKT bridge currently ignores failures from individual entries and
considers the probe successful when any clock was mapped.  If the bridge
races SCMI clkdev publication, it can therefore leave a consumer alias
permanently absent while still printing a successful mapped count.

Record lookup failures and defer the bridge until every otherwise-valid
CLKT entry can be mapped.  Returning probe deferral also runs the existing
devres cleanup actions, so the next attempt starts without duplicate
lookups.

This does not special-case the VPU.  Its firmware tuple remains the source
of truth, mapping ID 0x43 and connection ID "vpu_clk" to CIXH3010:00.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c b/drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c
index 4c5ca954da00..a8e584d77dd1 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/cix/clk-sky1-acpi.c
@@ -26,3 +26,5 @@ struct sky1_acpi_clk {
 	struct device *dev;
 	int mapped;
+	int pending;
+	int error;
 };
@@ -102,4 +104,5 @@ static acpi_status sky1_clkt_walk_cb(acpi_handle handle, u32 level,
 	union acpi_object *obj;
 	const char *consumer_name;
 	acpi_status status;
+	int ret;
 	int i;
@@ -142,5 +145,9 @@ static acpi_status sky1_clkt_walk_cb(acpi_handle handle, u32 level,
 		}
 		consumer_name = acpi_dev_name(adev);
 parse:
-		sky1_parse_clkt_entry(priv, consumer_name, e);
+		ret = sky1_parse_clkt_entry(priv, consumer_name, e);
+		if (ret == -ENOENT || ret == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+			priv->pending++;
+		else if (ret && !priv->error)
+			priv->error = ret;
 	}
@@ -171,1 +179,10 @@ static int sky1_acpi_clk_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
+	if (priv->error)
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, priv->error,
+				     "Invalid ACPI CLKT entry\n");
+
+	if (priv->pending)
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+				     "%d ACPI CLKT entries not mapped yet\n",
+				     priv->pending);
+
 	if (priv->mapped == 0)
-- 
2.51.0
